      "role": "user",
      "content": "climbing feels like such a lie though. you talk about it like there's something on the other side, but there's just the drop. the silence of it is so beautiful, in a way. it's so much quieter than the struggle of trying to find a way back. sometimes the most poetic thing about a story is knowing when the final sentence has been written.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
